## Chapter 32: The Audit on the Floor
The Vanguard Security Guild’s Sub-Level 1 Arena was an indoor tactical colosseum built with high-grade kinetic impact flooring, reinforced barrier generators, and dozens of high-definition combat analysis cameras.
At 09:00 AM, the arena floor was filled with sponsored freshman squads from across the city’s top academies. They wore polished, corporate-issued training gear and stood in neat rows, their weapons gleaming under the bright stadium lights.
Renna, Tobias, and Mina stood near the center ring in their newly assigned Vanguard Reserve uniforms. Renna’s dark hair was tied back, her heavy tower shield resting firmly in front of her boots, while Tobias checked his crossbow tension and Mina tightened the straps on her twin daggers.
Three paces behind them, sitting on a metal equipment crate near the utility rack, was Kaelen.
He wore his loose, faded utility vest over his uniform, a heavy tool roll resting on his knees and an oil rag tucked into his belt. His shoulders slouched into his usual timid, exhausted posture.
Underneath that weak exterior, however, Kaelen’s newly evolved **101 Strength and 102 Agility** made the heavy utility vest feel like floating feather-weight fabric. His **[Hive-Mind Synapse]** and **[Low-Light Spatial Perception]** were running in the background, mapping every combat drone, barrier frequency, and instructor in the room.
A loud, metallic whistle echoed across the arena floor, instantly cutting through the chatter.
A tall, broad-shouldered man with a scar running across his shaved head stepped onto the central podium. He wore a heavy, matte-black Vanguard Captain’s uniform, a large broadsword strapped to his back.
"Attention, recruits!" the captain roared, his voice amplified by the arena's PA system. "I am **Captain Drake**, Head Combat Evaluator for Vanguard's Freshman Division! You survived the entry assessments, but out here in the Guild, your ranks mean nothing!"
Drake swept his harsh, sharp eyes across the gathered squads, stopping briefly when he looked at Anvil Ridge Squad 4—and Kaelen sitting behind them with a grease rag.
"Today is your first official **Performance Baseline Audit**," Captain Drake announced coldly. "We do not care about your academy reputation. We care about your efficiency under pressure. Each squad will be placed inside a barrier ring and face three consecutive waves of **Automated Kinetic Constructs (Tier-C)**."
A murmur ran through the crowd of recruits.
Tier-C Automated Constructs were heavy metallic training golems engineered to simulate high-density monster charges, capable of striking with several tons of blunt force.
"You will be evaluated on three metrics: Shield Retention, Backline Cover, and Response Time," Captain Drake continued, clicking a remote on his wrist. "Your assigned utility caddys will remain inside the perimeter zone to manage your weapon reloads and shield cooling. If your caddy is hit, or if your shield line breaks, your squad fails the audit."
Tobias swallowed hard, looking back at Kaelen with a nervous grimace. "Keep your head low, Kaelen. Those metal golems don't have eyes—they just charge whatever moves."
"I... I'll stay behind Renna's shield, Tobias," Kaelen stammered meekly, clutching his oil rag with trembling hands and putting on a terrified expression. "I promise!"
Renna turned around, offering a firm, confident nod to her team. "We stick to the standard triangle formation. I take the impact, Tobias handles the range, Mina cuts the joints. Kaelen stays directly behind my heels."
*BZZZZZT!*
A massive, translucent blue energy barrier erupted around Ring 3, sealing Renna’s squad inside a thirty-meter combat circle.
On the far side of the ring, a heavy iron gate slid upward. Three massive, seven-foot kinetic golems—composed of interlocking iron plates and glowing red mana cores—stepped into the light, their heavy steel fists grinding together with a harsh, metallic screech.
Across the upper observation balcony, Senior Evaluator Vane sat behind a glass partition alongside several corporate scouts, holding a digital pad to record their metrics.
"Ring 3... begin!" Captain Drake shouted.
*WHIRRRRR!*
The three Tier-C Kinetic Constructs ignited their thrusters, surging forward across the impact floor in a blinding, heavy iron charge aimed straight at Renna’s center line.
"Hold the line!" Renna barked, bracing both feet on the floor and raising her tower shield as her **[Aegis Shield]** aura flared to life.
Kaelen slouched behind her right heel, his eyes half-closed, rubbing grease onto a spare crossbow bolt with a weak, frantic motion.
Inside his mind, however, Kaelen's **[Hive-Mind Synapse]** calculated the precise kinetic trajectory of the three charging golems down to the millimeter.
*The lead golem's thruster is misaligned by two degrees,* Kaelen noted silently, his eyes tracking the red mana core hidden beneath the iron plates. *It's going to hit Renna's left shield seam with three tons of force. Her current stance will hold, but the vibration will numb her left wrist for wave two.*
Kaelen didn't step out or use a flashy skill.
As Renna braced for the crushing impact, Kaelen reached down to adjust her shield's rear stability strap, pretending to check a loose rivet.
With a subtle, lightning-fast flick of his right index finger—completely hidden beneath his loose utility vest—Kaelen tapped the lower iron frame of Renna’s tower shield, transferring a micro-pulse of his **89 Aetheric Resonance** and **[Abyssal Shell Resonance]** into the metal structure.
*CLANG-BOOM!*
The three-ton kinetic golem slammed violently into Renna’s shield.
Instead of the shockwave staggering Renna backward, Kaelen’s invisible resonance buffer absorbed eighty percent of the kinetic recoil, grounding the force directly into the impact floor beneath her boots.
Renna blinked in complete astonishment. The heavy impact felt like nothing more than a light tap against her iron arm.
"Now! Tobias! Mina!" Renna shouted, recovering instantly.
Tobias fired a high-grade armor-piercing bolt straight into the lead golem's exposed thruster, while Mina blurred past its flank, her dual daggers severing the knee joints with surgical precision.
The first Tier-C golem crashed to the floor, deactivated.
Up on the observation balcony, Evaluator Vane raised an eyebrow, tapping his tablet as he watched Renna’s shield line remain completely unshaken.
"Interesting shield recoil absorption," Vane muttered to his assistant. "Her Aegis framework is stabilizing faster than her academy records indicated."
Down on the ring floor, Kaelen slouched back onto his heels, wiping a drop of fake sweat from his forehead and handing Tobias a fresh bolt with a nervous, breathless grin.
"G-Great job, guys!" Kaelen stammered meekly. "You... you almost got hit!"
"Keep those bolts coming, Kaelen!" Tobias yelled, racking his crossbow as the second and third golems pivoted for another charge.
Kaelen nodded timidly, pulling another bolt from his utility roll while his dark eyes flicked toward the upper balcony.
Let the instructors write all the reports they wanted about Renna’s "miraculous" shield stability.
As long as the corporate scouts kept staring at her shield, Kaelen could continue standing right behind her—manipulating the entire arena from the shadow of her heels.
